# Guest: fstests
# Joined with the profile of the filesystem under test, as in
# fstests+xfs-filesystem (docs/tasks/kernel.rst, "The configuration").
# Beside the guest's own, each fragment builds what a fstests test needs:
# core/namespaces.config PID namespaces (xfs/667), core/boot-config.config
# BSD process accounting (generic/596), storage/scsi-debug.config
# (generic/108), storage/nvdimm.config persistent memory (generic/462),
# mem/swap.config swap files (generic/493), fs/ext4.config ext2 (xfs/049),
# fs/overlayfs.config (generic/699), security/selinux.config SELinux
# (generic/700), storage/scsi-tape.config and storage/iscsi-tcp.config a
# tape over iSCSI (xfs/035), debug/hung-task.config the hung-task
# detector the machine panics on, and debug/tracing.config ftrace
# (xfs/559).
